WEBVTT

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.000
"#20    Another Chance"

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.500
"#20    Another Chance"
I'm going to quit teaching
your koto club as of today.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.250
What's the reason?

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.160
I no longer feel like I'm
good enough to teach them.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:03.080
You warned me about this
at the beginning, right?

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:10.250
If there's anything we can do,
we definitely would like to be of help.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.660
I came to recommend

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.910
my granddaughter Akira
as your outside instructor.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.450
Outside instructor...

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:19.830
This is Akira's career record.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:25.200
By the way, she doesn't have to get paid.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.830
What? But that's just not...

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.660
Teaching others is a great
learning experience in itself.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.620
It's going to help her in the future, too, so...

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:38.580
What do you think, Mr. Takinami?

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:41.000
I was just thinking about finding someone

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.950
who can give them koto lessons.

00:02:42.950 --> 00:02:45.580
So if you could help us, that would be great.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.750
However...

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.000
...if I find you useless,
I'll ask you to quit right away.

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.950
Would that be okay with you?

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:56.540
I know I'm being rude.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:59.120
But the instructor's compatibility with
the students and her quality as a teacher

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.000
will greatly affect their future performances.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.910
I believe that our club can go to nationals.

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:11.450
My students have the potential.

00:03:11.450 --> 00:03:15.910
So if they couldn't go to nationals
just because of an inadequate instructor,

00:03:15.910 --> 00:03:17.330
it wouldn't be funny.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.330
"Inadequate"?

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.500
That's fine.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:26.450
It's okay to fire me the moment
you feel that I'm not good enough.

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:35.790
I did say that, but I don't think
you're not good enough.

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:38.200
But I feel that way about myself.

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.080
If the teacher can't teach with confidence,

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.620
it'll have a negative influence
on the students.

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.250
I see... Understood.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:50.000
Since you're teaching them without pay,
I can't force you to continue.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.200
I'm sorry to see you go, though.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:56.120
But could you stay at least until
I find the next instructor?

00:03:56.120 --> 00:03:58.450
I'll find someone as soon as possible.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:00.200
Okay.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.580
Well then...

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:06.410
Although it was a short period of time,
I'm glad we had you.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:09.830
You've helped them improve
their skills quite a bit.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.000
"Koto Club"
Thank you very much.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:18.910
What was that? Sarcasm?

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:22.120
If anything, they all disliked me...

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:35.250
"Koto Club"

00:04:41.290 --> 00:04:44.200
What...? Their sound is...

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.950
Miss Dojima?

00:04:54.950 --> 00:04:56.540
Your sound...

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:02.000
It's only been a few days,
but your sound changed quite a bit.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.120
You think so?!

00:05:03.120 --> 00:05:05.080
Did something happen?

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.250
We listened to your performance.

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.200
We did think it might be a bit rude
listening to it without asking you, but...

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:15.950
I'm sorry.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:20.790
But after we finished listening
to your performance together,

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:23.450
we all stood up without saying anything

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:26.910
and started practicing like crazy.

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:32.660
When we heard your performance,
we all suddenly realized...

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:38.200
...what it means to
"play every single note with care."

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.330
Miss Dojima! I can now play that spot
you taught me the other day!

00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:43.410
Listen!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.250
"Please."

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.290
Please!

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.000
--How was that?!
--The rhythm isn't right.

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:05.950
But I can see you're now putting
lots of care into the sound. I'm surprised.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:10.580
All right!

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.200
You look happy, Kota.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.620
I rarely get compliments from teachers, so...

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.040
A-After you taught me
how to position my arm,

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.040
pressing the strings became easier.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.450
Thank you... very much.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:32.540
I can even hear "stop" now,
even when you're not around.

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.370
Satowa...

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:42.250
U-Um... Could you give us advice
on our ensemble as well today?

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:49.620
We have been practicing it when you're
not around and during after-club practice.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:53.620
But.... Um...

00:06:53.620 --> 00:06:56.540
I-I'm not good at teaching, so...!

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:02.040
We stumble from the start
and can't play it well together at all.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:06.290
But I don't know what to do,
so we can't move forward.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.790
So... um...

00:07:08.790 --> 00:07:12.040
Hey! Are you indirectly complaining about us?!

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:14.540
N-No! I don't mean that at all!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.330
What are you saying I should teach you?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.750
Even after I pushed her away like that...

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:29.080
You're right.
You're disorganized from the start.

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:36.580
Let's pair the solo and 17-string,
and the first and second kotos

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.290
and practice separately first.

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:43.330
In this piece, the 17-string is
the foundation and the solo is the key.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:48.160
So first, please form a consistent core
with these two parts together.

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.410
"Core"...

00:07:49.410 --> 00:07:52.290
Wow! You guys are over the moon!

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.450
If you consider the 17-string and the solo
as the "root" and "trunk" of a tree,

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:00.540
the first and second kotos are leaves
and blossoms that lend colors to it.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.040
Depending on how the first and
second kotos are played together,

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:05.910
the expression of the piece
changes quite a bit.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.410
The first and second koto parts
chase each other a lot

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:11.660
and have lots of interplay,

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:13.870
so you should also practice together.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.540
Then after that,
we'll go back to the ensemble.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:20.540
Well then, let's start with
the 17-string and the solo.

00:08:20.540 --> 00:08:22.580
O-Okay.

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:30.330
Stop. The 17-string is being
influenced by the solo again.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.330
Sorry, Chika. It was me.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:35.370
I'm sorry! Can we try again?

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:39.040
I thought I nailed it after practicing hard.

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.500
Sorry! I wanna try that spot one more time!

00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.120
Okay.

00:08:46.120 --> 00:08:50.450
So just mixing in the solo
makes it this much harder to play?

00:08:50.450 --> 00:08:53.580
Shoot... Considering the structure of the piece,

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:56.660
I paired the 17-string and
the solo without thinking much,

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:57.700
but...

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.080
...it might've put him
in a very tough situation.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.250
This is a tricky bar with irregular eighth notes.

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:11.450
And the solo coming in
with triplets makes it even harder.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:13.660
Can we try again?!

00:09:14.870 --> 00:09:17.620
Dammit... I'm dragging them down.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:22.830
Chika can play it without difficulty.
I don't want to keep holding them back!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.950
Am I listening to the solo too much?

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:28.000
But I <i>should </i>listen to it, right?
Since it's an ensemble.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.290
But it won't work if I get influenced.
I need to focus on my own sound.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:35.750
I'm fine up to here...

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:36.830
Next...!

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.660
Dammit!

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.830
Sorry!

00:09:40.830 --> 00:09:43.620
Should I ask them to let me
practice alone for now?

00:09:43.620 --> 00:09:47.910
No. It's pointless if I can't
play along with the solo.

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:59.370
Oh, no... If this situation continues...

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:02.080
L-Let's move on for--

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.500
One more time.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:05.750
What?

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.700
We'll try one more time.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.750
Starting from the same spot.

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.910
I'm sorry, Miss Dojima!

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.950
Can I keep trying until I can do it?!

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:30.950
Chika! Hozuki!
Sorry, but play along with me!

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:32.000
Strawberry au lait.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.000
I'll treat you!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:35.500
One strawberry au lait per mistake.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:36.500
You bastard!

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:37.660
Paplico would do, too.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:39.410
You slimy bastard!

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:43.330
Keishi...

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.040
"Strawberry Au Lait"
Keishi...

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:49.750
How can I be first place like you?

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.580
"Strawberry Au Lait"

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:04.580
I failed many times and I even
injured myself a little...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.250
...but I kept trying to do it, and I did it!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.660
All right! I did it!

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:39.120
Sorry, Chika! Guess I won't be treating you
to many strawberry au laits.

00:11:43.870 --> 00:11:46.200
Whoooa! Wh-Wh-Wh-What's wrong,
Miss Dojima?!

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:48.870
Wh-What happened?!

00:11:48.870 --> 00:11:52.910
Well, it's... I'm sorry. It's nothing.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:59.870
H-Here! A handkerchief! Tissue!

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.870
Um...

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:12.410
I do appreciate your thoughtfulness,
but I don't need this many.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:15.040
Oh, o-of course!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.040
Sorry!

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.370
Wh-Why did she cry out of the blue?
Is it because I'm so terrible?

00:12:19.370 --> 00:12:22.370
I don't know!
Women often cry out of the blue.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:26.370
Um... It's really nothing.
I just got some dust in my eye.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.250
Oh, yeah?!

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:29.870
It's painful when that happens.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.080
Don't scare us like that.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:32.500
It was just some dust.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:35.870
I'm sorry to scare you like that.

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.830
Well then, let's move on.

00:12:57.870 --> 00:13:00.040
Hey... What kind of practice
are you guys doing?

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.370
We're practicing in two groups.
The 17-string and solo,

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:04.290
and the first and second kotos.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:05.950
I see.

00:13:10.580 --> 00:13:13.290
Ugh! I'm the only one out of sync again!

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:17.700
Sorry. To think that I still get out of sync
even when using a metronome...

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:21.330
Don't worry, Kota. You'll be fine.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:23.370
Hm? What're you doing, Suzu?

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:26.290
I forbid you guys to use
the metronome from here on.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:27.160
What?!

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:30.080
Oh, no! When my sense of rhythm
is already bad enough...!

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:33.910
Since your sense of rhythm is already bad,
this won't make much difference.

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:35.120
That's mean!

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:35.910
Besides, there's no metronome sound
included in the piece.

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:39.120
"Tenkyu"
Besides, there's no metronome sound
included in the piece.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.370
"Tenkyu"
Don't desperately try to match the sound
that doesn't exist in the piece.

00:13:42.370 --> 00:13:44.410
Match the others' sound.

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.290
That's the ensemble.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:48.790
So...

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.450
Miss Dojima...

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:52.330
...and Hozuki...

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:55.660
Can you two show the others
a good example of an ensemble?

00:13:55.660 --> 00:13:59.410
I want Miss Dojima to play
the 17-string and Hozuki the solo.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:00.500
I wanna hear it!

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:01.950
Yeah! Me, too!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.330
What? Um...

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:07.620
Well, these guys can get it quicker
by hearing music instead of an explanation.

00:14:07.620 --> 00:14:10.160
So can you?

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.870
I'd like to ask you, too!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:16.540
I-I'd like to play... with you.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.500
Okay.

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:25.660
Come to think of it,

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.620
I've never seen Hozuki
playing with anyone else.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:33.290
I wonder if it'll be different depending
on who she plays with...

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:59.750
Our sounds... expand...

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.290
They come together...

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:03.750
And a new sound is born.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.370
We come to know each other.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.620
And we accept and improve each other...

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:14.910
Ever further and deeper...
our sounds become one piece...

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:16.910
They become one world.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.950
Mr. Suzu!

00:15:41.950 --> 00:15:45.870
So the ensemble is... The ensemble
is all about an interchange of hearts?!

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:48.620
That's something you're good at, right?

00:15:48.620 --> 00:15:52.330
Thanks to Miss Dojima's lessons, you're
getting better at facing a single note.

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:55.080
Your technique and foundation
are better, too.

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:59.750
You're now probably ready to practice
together, but don't just play together.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:03.330
See the entire piece thoroughly.
Understand its flow.

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.790
Think how your own sound goes
together with others' in that flow.

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:10.620
Think about what your
sound means and its role.

00:16:10.620 --> 00:16:13.750
What you say is always too difficult.

00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:15.750
I don't understand it at all.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.450
Agonize over it.

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:21.000
Agonize, think... and intently face it.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:25.950
The more you do, the thicker and
deeper your sound will resonate.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:31.750
Yeah! I'm getting fired up!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.950
Okay, now get back to your practice already.

00:16:40.290 --> 00:16:42.870
That's all for today.
Please put your kotos away.

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:45.200
Thank you for your lesson!

00:16:45.200 --> 00:16:47.200
Hey, about the after-club practice today...

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:48.450
Yeah?

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:53.910
Um... Satowa mentioned it, too,
but what is this "after-club practice"?

00:16:53.910 --> 00:16:57.200
There's this nice instrument shop
that lets us play there with their kotos

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.660
so we can practice after the club.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.830
What? You'll practice more after this?

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:06.200
You practice early morning
and during lunch break, too, right?

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.700
Yes, we're immersed in koto.

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:11.580
But it's fun. A lot of fun.

00:17:11.580 --> 00:17:15.120
You all must really like the koto.

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:18.500
So must you, right?

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.250
Welcome home, Akira.

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.870
How are things in the club?

00:17:25.870 --> 00:17:29.540
Isn't it about time for the club members
to throw in the towel?

00:17:29.540 --> 00:17:34.870
I investigated the club a little.
That really is a low-ranked one.

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:38.200
It's a haunt for delinquents. How disgusting.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:43.290
I bet none of them are serious
about the koto anyway, right?

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.540
To think that girl is hanging out
with a crowd like that...

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:50.620
She sure has hit rock bottom. Right, Aki--

00:17:52.500 --> 00:17:55.160
Akira?

00:17:55.160 --> 00:18:01.120
I'm sorry, Grandmother. I'm exhausted today.
May I go to bed now?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.160
Of course you may.

00:18:12.250 --> 00:18:14.330
Hey, Chika!

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.660
Don't sleep there!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:20.040
Hey, did you hear me?
You're gonna catch a-- Whoa!

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:22.000
Hey, you are up?

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:23.250
What're you listening to?

00:18:23.250 --> 00:18:25.160
My own performance.

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:29.120
Say, Isaki. What do you think I lack?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.830
What? Is there anything you don't lack?

00:18:32.830 --> 00:18:35.910
Oh yeah, sugar.
You're always eating sweet stuff.

00:18:35.910 --> 00:18:38.200
You stupid head.

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.790
Quit sulking.

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:41.120
You damn hag.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.410
--What'd you say, you damn brat?!

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:43.080
--So when Hozuki plays with
someone at her skill level,
--What'd you say, you damn brat?!

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:46.120
--So when Hozuki plays with
someone at her skill level,
--I'm not that old!

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:48.250
it turns out like that, huh...?

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.370
It was really good.

00:18:50.370 --> 00:18:52.540
It seemed Hozuki was having
an easy time playing,

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:56.410
and her performance was better
than usual as well.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:59.700
Think about what your sound
means and its role.

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:04.290
"The Hozuki School"

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.750
You all must really like the koto.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.700
So must you, right?

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:19.330
"Teachers' Room"

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.790
Mr. Takinami.

00:19:20.790 --> 00:19:24.790
Miss Dojima. I thought you
didn't have a lesson today.

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:27.580
I'm sorry, but I need to talk to you.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:28.660
Talk to me?

00:19:28.660 --> 00:19:33.160
Yes, but before that, there's something
I'd like to check with you.

00:19:33.160 --> 00:19:34.950
What is it?

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:40.660
How serious are you
about aiming for nationals?

00:19:40.660 --> 00:19:45.000
When I met you the first time,
I thought you were serious.

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:47.870
But you don't come to see the practices at all.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:51.830
And then, you suddenly show up
and give them advice like yesterday.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.450
Are you doing things on a whim?

00:19:54.450 --> 00:19:59.910
Well, I don't really care what you think,
but I <i>am </i>very serious.

00:19:59.910 --> 00:20:02.700
I thought I wasn't needed
for practicing the basics,

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.370
so I just let you handle it.

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:07.000
Let me handle it?

00:20:07.000 --> 00:20:11.620
You still taught them properly
without me being there, right?

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:14.080
I-I did...

00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:17.040
But you're entrusting your
students with a stranger...

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:18.200
I feel you aren't serious after all.

00:20:18.200 --> 00:20:19.620
For two years...

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:20.500
What?

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:26.080
For two years, you've seriously faced
a single piece and produced a result.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:31.120
You even told me to fire you when
I feel you're not good enough.

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:35.620
With that kind of resolution, it's harder
to think of a reason <i>not </i>to trust you.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:43.410
Is that all you needed to talk about?
Well then, I have a class to teach, so...

00:20:43.410 --> 00:20:47.000
Please let me... be of help one more time!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:53.500
I'm sorry. I just told you yesterday
that I was going to quit.

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:56.700
I know I'm really causing trouble.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:21:00.290
I might not be good enough after all.

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:05.080
But please...! Could you give me
another chance?!

00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:25.580
Thank you. Welcome back.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:32.540
It definitely wasn't a waste of time.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:41.580
The time I spent then is giving me
the power to stand here right now.

00:21:41.580 --> 00:21:44.040
It was never a waste of time.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:49.000
Hey, you. Have you seen Akira?

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:52.330
She went out early this morning.

00:21:52.330 --> 00:21:55.370
What...? I see.

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:58.660
Don't tell me she is...

00:22:01.660 --> 00:22:08.040
To be sure... Maybe I'll take action
before it's too late.

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:52.120
Next time, "Meaning and Role."

00:23:52.120 --> 00:23:54.450
"#21    Meaning and Role"
